Direct3D 10: do not end a render condition that was never begun

Direct3D sets "no predicate" whenever it clears the device's state, and the driver passed that
on each time. On virgl the host answers an end without a begin with an OpenGL error, counts
it as an error of the context and from then on skips every clear, draw and copy of that
context without a word: a program that cleared its state once drew nothing afterwards.

diff -ru a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Query.cpp b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Query.cpp
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Query.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Query.cpp
@@ -350,7 +350,12 @@
    wait = (pQuery && pQuery->Flags & D3D10DDI_QUERY_MISCFLAG_PREDICATEHINT) ?
              PIPE_RENDER_COND_NO_WAIT : PIPE_RENDER_COND_WAIT;
 
-   pipe->render_condition(pipe, state, PredicateValue, wait);
+   /* Ending a condition that was never begun is not harmless everywhere. Direct3D does it
+    * whenever it clears the device's state; virgl's host makes an OpenGL error of it, and from
+    * then on drops everything the context draws.
+    */
+   if (state || pDevice->pPredicate)
+      pipe->render_condition(pipe, state, PredicateValue, wait);
 
    pDevice->pPredicate = pQuery;
    pDevice->PredicateValue = PredicateValue;
